From ec74bbbca3ada2b879024b1d8c4703e152f789ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): right-size sparse-MLA head block and
 multi-segment decode wave bound

Cap SparseMlaV41Plan.routes block_H to the 16-head MMA multiple covering local
heads and scale threads accordingly so 16-head ranks (TP3 rank 2 after
_trim_padded_groups and all TP4 ranks) run extend and decode with a 16-head,
128-thread CTA instead of padding to 32 heads and 256 threads and discarding
half the warps. Add an explicit skip_inactive flag on sparse_mla_fwd_v41 so
multi-wave decode still skips inactive segments and dead rows when block_H is
16 while single-wave split remains branch-free. On multi-segment indexed
layers, keep segment-split decode until unsplit extend fills a full wave of SMs
(rows <= sms // head_blocks = 48 on GB10) while leaving single-segment SWA
layers unchanged.

Base: 1107 patch head c47b54ae471a24b830e3515212b8c0bf5ee14604, tree
13e4781d19bc4a18b0d3d4daad7921c465e3355e, on upstream
19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354.
Quality: 100% bit-identical output and exact precision preserved. segment_chunks
(4), block_I (32), FP32 accumulators, FOLD rounding order, and wo_input rotation
and quantization are unchanged. Peak workspace memory across target and drafter
lanes is unchanged.
Tests: test_sparse_mla_plan_routes_right_sizes_head_block_and_decode_waves and
offline SM121 TileLang lowering + PDL verification across all 12 route variants.
Upstream status: prepared for review against the pinned candidate source; not
submitted to the canonical upstream and not promoted.
